html_url":"https://github.com/jonexai999","id":306697508,"login":"jonexai999","node_id":"U_kgDOEkfVJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/36f8e05dadfedfa69f3732d3d41a813ae9dd8f60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:34:29Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai999"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:17:58Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai999"},"message":"1. feat(object-storage): S3-compatible object storage — S3/MinIO/COS backends with STS credential cache, direct uploads and presigned access across Knowledge Base / RAG / MCP workflows\n2. feat(quota): system-wide knowledge base quotas — file/KB/tenant-level limits with atomic concurrent checks, usage indicators and limit-based action blocking\n3. feat(answer-feedback): answer feedback and issue tracking — likes/dislikes, comments, idempotent operations, snapshots and feedback statistics\n4. feat(knowledge-base): membership and quota services, admin role guard, SystemMonitor page and session-expired handling\n5. feat(deploy): nginx http/https access modes with TLS support, frontend-gateway mode script and updated nginx layout\n6. fix(security): test-token bypass gated behind ENABLE_TEST_TOKENS (default off); GATEWAY_API_KEY sentinel with startup guard; placeholder defaults for DB/Neo4j/MinIO credentials\n7. chore: rename legacy product branding to Jonex across UI and code; clean up obsolete modules","tree":{"sha":"4b038734874e08ba7126d8d94979ad95dd62b20f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/trees/4b038734874e08ba7126d8d94979ad95dd62b20f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/commits/36f8e05dadfedfa69f3732d3d41a813ae9dd8f60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306697508?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonexai999","id":306697508,"login":"jonexai999","node_id":"U_kgDOEkfVJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yuezhiai/jonex/commit/36f8e05dadfedfa69f3732d3d41a813ae9dd8f60","node_id":"C_kwDOTdBTz9oAKDM2ZjhlMDVkYWRmZWRmYTY5ZjM3MzJkM2Q0MWE4MTNhZTlkZDhmNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yuezhiai/jonex/commit/a8eb6f653cbc55df478d4be9bf98e0a1aba75475","sha":"a8eb6f653cbc55df478d4be9bf98e0a1aba75475","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/a8eb6f653cbc55df478d4be9bf98e0a1aba75475"}],"sha":"36f8e05dadfedfa69f3732d3d41a813ae9dd8f60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/36f8e05dadfedfa69f3732d3d41a813ae9dd8f60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306697508?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonexai999","id":306697508,"login":"jonexai999","node_id":"U_kgDOEkfVJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/a8eb6f653cbc55df478d4be9bf98e0a1aba75475/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T08:34:35Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T08:34:35Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"message":"1. feat(object-storage): S3-compatible object storage — added an S3 backend, enabled direct uploads and presigned\n  access across Knowledge Base, RAG, and MCP workflows, and generated CSP rules dynamically for COS, S3, and MinIO\n  2. fix(storage-security): STS and COS multi-tenant hardening — blocked wildcard injection through tenant IDs,\n  consolidated STS credential caching, bounded presigning locks and client caches, corrected expiration semantics,\n  and enforced tenant-specific object prefixes\n  3. feat(image-reference): image reference pipeline — completed image asset uploads, presigned URLs, thumbnail and\n  full-size image access, layout-aware topic anchors, batched reranking, low-quality reference filtering, and\n  fallback handling for missing asset_url values\n  4. perf(ai-runtime): VLM and ontology-search latency controls — introduced dedicated VLM concurrency limits, fixed\n  image-context injection, added reasoning-depth controls, and reduced the impact of reasoning models on parsing and\n  retrieval latency\n  5. refactor(atomic-rag): Atomic RAG v1 retirement — removed the legacy graph reader and v1 LightRAG adapter, and\n  standardized the platform on the v2 query contract, client, and HTTP LightRAG integration\n  6. feat(answer-feedback): answer feedback and issue-tracking loop — added answer-level likes and dislikes,\n  comments, idempotent operations, version control, and answer/reference/reasoning snapshots, together with feedback\n  statistics, adoption, deletion, and fallback KB ID resolution\n  7. feat(knowledge-search): retrieval scope and result details — ultimately restricted retrieval to the current\n  domain space, filtered domain-service candidates by accessible knowledge bases, and added strict mode, API-backed\n  ontology details, and on-demand chunk loading\n  8. feat(quota): system-wide knowledge base quotas — introduced file-, knowledge-base-, and tenant-level limits,\n  used advisory locks for atomic concurrent checks, and added usage indicators, limit-based action blocking, and\n  dynamic file-size validation in the UI\n  9. feat(document-management): document batch operations and reprocessing — added batch downloads, configurable\n  page sizes, uploads defaulting to the current folder, and migration audit logs; reparsing now clears stale error\n  counts and distinguishes OpenKB recompilation from ontology re-extraction\n  10. fix(knowledge-base): knowledge base binding and capability cleanup — stopped automatically binding new\n  knowledge bases to the first domain service, removed redundant ontology binding and compilation logic, and\n  filtered parser and ingestion options to active entries\n  11. feat(mcp-key): unified MCP Key model — consolidated standard and write keys into the mcp_keys table, unified\n  service permissions, write_grants, statuses, notes, expiration, revocation, and recreation responses, and added\n  auditable soft deletion\n  12. fix(mcp-authz): MCP authorization hardening — revalidated write grants when changing spaces, rejected key\n  creation or updates with no authorization, deduplicated writable knowledge bases, filtered service directories by\n  key scope, and closed cross-space authorization leaks\n  13. feat(mcp-service): MCP Tool publishing and connection details — enabled Tool configuration in the MCP\n  integration UI, required confirmation when renaming published Tools, blocked publishing when Tool metadata was\n  incomplete, and standardized API/MCP URLs and transport information\n  14. refactor(mcp-upload): direct-upload protocol — removed inline Base64 uploads in favor of object-storage\n  uploads followed by confirm_upload, expanded support for valid filename characters, and removed unused internal\n  upload endpoints\n  15. feat(auth): tenant-aware login, impersonation, and security policies — made tenant selection mandatory at\n  login, added secure tenant impersonation for platform administrators, and introduced failed-login lockout, minimum\n  password length, and session timeout settings\n  16. feat(user-management): tenant and user management improvements — loaded roles according to the target tenant,\n  allowed optional password changes when editing users, rejected whitespace in key tenant and user fields, and\n  removed the tenant plan-type field\n  17. feat(rbac): layered knowledge base authorization — introduced viewer, editor, kb_manager, and search-oriented\n  access, exempted tenant administrators from space filtering, removed separate domain-service permission\n  management, and standardized frontend checks through usePermission and PermButton\n  18. refactor(domain-template): streamlined domain template management — removed publishing, compilation preview,\n  and impacted-KB actions from the frontend while retaining scenario, object, relationship, constraint, and YAML\n  editing; also standardized “Domain Template” terminology and fixed stale cards after renaming\n  19. fix(prompt-template): automatic prompt versioning — removed manual version input, switched to integer versions\n  that increment only when content changes, displayed the current version in the editor, and corrected existing\n  version data\n  20. feat(navigation): reorganized application navigation — restructured the main menu around Domain Ontology, Data\n  Engine, Integration Extensions, and Platform Management, and reassigned entries such as the MCP ecosystem to their\n  appropriate sections\n  21. refactor(frontend-request): unified frontend request and error handling — standardized tokens, language\n  headers, response envelopes, and concurrent 401 handling across Shell, Core Business, Ecosystem Management, and\n  Platform Management; page-level handlers now prioritize backend err.message details\n  22. build(deploy): controlled migrations and more reliable image builds — added version tracking through\n  schema_migrations, changed incremental migrations to an explicitly triggered workflow with dry-run support,\n  enabled domestic and international mirror selection, and fixed workspace resolution, APT sources, Vite aliases,\n  and configurable proxy timeouts","tree":{"sha":"b50ea0770d9a768426f0af717032732e656b0959","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/trees/b50ea0770d9a768426f0af717032732e656b0959"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/commits/a8eb6f653cbc55df478d4be9bf98e0a1aba75475","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306697508?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c