er}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/41e1ff38b74d1c0941e96bcdc9d497b238263644/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:25:15Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:25:15Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"message":"1. feat(rbac): RBAC permission system — fine-grained permission codes replace hardcoded admin checks, permission-driven sidebar menu & user-role binding, admin endpoint guards, drop legacy permission seeds\n2. fix(auth): auth hardening — require_admin no-op missing JWT auth, get_current_user jonex_test_ token special-case, per-tenant role loading in user management\n3. feat(mcp): MCP access-key convergence — domain service API keys + knowledge write keys, permissions read/write/*→call/view, hash-lookup auth replacing bypassable prefix check, space isolation, 4-state lifecycle with disable/recreate\n4. feat(mcp): MCP management UI rework — 3-step key wizard drawer, detail drawer redesign, admin-only menu tightening & precise permission mapping, search_mix hybrid retrieval tool\n5. feat(kb): KB space authorization — viewer/editor overlay grants, has_space_role entry, multi-entry fallback checks on execute/delete, i18n error keys\n6. feat(rag-table): table parsing & chunking governance — L1-L4 grid/header-inference/dual-merge/context-header, Row-as-Object, stub/low-quality filtering, dual-direction adjudication, in-row cell split, gray-release fixes\n7. feat(rag-text-block): text block packing governance — C4 gate, continued-block page-number fixes\n8. feat(kb): search history snapshot replay — answer/reference/reasoning-chain snapshots, cap cleanup & no-overwrite, strictConfig reuse, paginated \"view more\"\n9. feat(kb): retrieval quality fixes — RAG subject-filter soft weighting, platform answer ownership, KB display-name source labels in fusion prompt, 500 on deleted-KB traversal\n10. feat(kb): image reference chain — §image-refs P0~P3\n11. feat(openkb): OpenKB/LLM-Wiki schema — compile settings & version fencing, compiled-status column & filter, wiki page tree/graph browsing, dual-pipeline transcript gap fixes\n12. feat(kb): document library batch ops — multi-file upload, folder move/batch-move & counts, default data-source init for new KB, upload timezone fix\n13. fix(gateway): proxy route fixes — KB folder/tag double-prefix 404, register MCP key/write-key/role-user passthrough routes\n14. fix(frontend): rendering & styles — Markdown/GFM fragment rendering, shared cssinjs cache fixing dropdown styles, viewport-adaptive heights, layout overflow fixes\n15. chore(deploy): PostgreSQL Debian image + incremental migration runner (idempotent update/) + permission/role sequence alignment","tree":{"sha":"2b3f60d376e416ab796d9121c11c0fbab9d9c6eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/trees/2b3f60d376e416ab796d9121c11c0fbab9d9c6eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/git/commits/41e1ff38b74d1c0941e96bcdc9d497b238263644","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306697508?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonexai999","id":306697508,"login":"jonexai999","node_id":"U_kgDOEkfVJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yuezhiai/jonex/commit/41e1ff38b74d1c0941e96bcdc9d497b238263644","node_id":"C_kwDOTdBTz9oAKDQxZTFmZjM4Yjc0ZDFjMDk0MWU5NmJjZGM5ZDQ5N2IyMzgyNjM2NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yuezhiai/jonex/commit/f6205dcd3ef1052bfc9930929f84a1fadbaf4901","sha":"f6205dcd3ef1052bfc9930929f84a1fadbaf4901","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/f6205dcd3ef1052bfc9930929f84a1fadbaf4901"}],"sha":"41e1ff38b74d1c0941e96bcdc9d497b238263644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/41e1ff38b74d1c0941e96bcdc9d497b238263644"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306697508?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonexai999","id":306697508,"login":"jonexai999","node_id":"U_kgDOEkfVJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonexai999","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yuezhiai/jonex/commits/f6205dcd3ef1052bfc9930929f84a1fadbaf4901/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:55:57Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:55:57Z","email":"jonexai@hotmail.com","name":"jonexai"},"message":"feat: standalone MCP server, KB retrieval & reliability overhaul\n\nSquashed several dozen commits from the source branch into this one.\n\n1. MCP server — now its own containerized service. Keys moved to CRUD +\n   JWT management with separate write/call/read permissions and two-level\n   rate limiting. The upload/status/list/search tools only reach callers\n   through the Gateway''s internal invoke, and downloads go through a\n   tokenized proxy so raw storage URLs never leak.\n\n2. OpenKB / LLM-Wiki — gained a full compilation pipeline and a Wiki read\n   mode, with reasoning-chain tracing and reparse/recompile support, and\n   the pipeline_type -> kb_type terms are now consistent everywhere.\n\n3. Retrieval — quality got a real push: P1/P2 reworked with strict and\n   deep paths, search_mix mixed dispatch, and a multi-KB recall panel.\n\n4. Knowledge-base reliability — overhauled: stale-task cleanup,\n   recoverable task handles, a heartbeat fix, row-level chunking for\n   tables, and duplicate-upload validation.\n\n5. Ontology RAG — now carries chunk-level references, stores\n   merge/relation data as JSON, aggregates multi-hop queries in Cypher,\n   and OntoRAG latency is noticeably down.\n\n6. Security — hardened across the board: Redis fallback, hash-collision\n   expunge, audit backoff, KB access control, and COS URL hardening.\n\n7. Audit / telemetry — gained a ResourceType enum, a resource_id fix, and\n   wider usage-log dimensions.\n\n8. Frontend — on a single toolchain now: pnpm workspace, unified\n   tsconfig/vite baselines, MobX -> Zustand, eslint/prettier/husky,\n   extracted shared-lib and i18n packages, and a new MCP Key management\n   page.\n\n9. Deploy — now includes shared-lib in the Docker build, ships env\n   templates, and makes the mirror switches configurable.","tree":{"sha":"53f96