lt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/ad03d6acf37bbf04fbe5b82f34e0a66cfda458a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T23:53:51Z","email":"emunluturk@gmail.com","name":"Mehmet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T23:53:51Z","email":"emunluturk@gmail.com","name":"Mehmet"},"message":"fix(github): clippy question_mark, cache race, scraping-flag false positive\n\n- limited_suffix: rewrite else-if-let as ?-operator to match retry_wait''s\n  existing shape and clear the new clippy::question_mark warning.\n- scan_pass_with_progress_cancellable: gate the clean-repo cache save on a\n  run-local saw_cancel flag instead of re-reading the shared cancel\n  AtomicBool. The desktop clears that shared flag at the start of every new\n  scan, so a slow run''s save gate could otherwise run after a newer scan\n  cleared it, poisoning the cache with cancel-skipped repos recorded as\n  clean. Added a regression test that reproduces the race via on_progress\n  (which fires after each repo''s result and before the save gate).\n- errors.ts: anchor the anti-scraping-flag match on \"scraping github\"\n  instead of bare \"scraping\" — a RateLimited message embeds the request\n  URL, which can contain a repo name like \"me/web-scraping-kit\" and was\n  misclassifying plain rate limits as the abuse flag.","tree":{"sha":"0d3d159e16b22cad096e7e52f3f608a16767bb32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/0d3d159e16b22cad096e7e52f3f608a16767bb32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/