"date":"2026-07-21T13:32:54Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"feat(core): scan the hiding spots — pnpm .pnpm store, bun cache, build output (FP-clean)\n\nCloses the \"malware hides in cache/build dirs\" gap the FP hunt raised — WITHOUT the\nstructural-FP flood that made those dirs excluded in the first place (a probe showed\n452/832 legit bundles trip the capability gate).\n\n- scan_node_modules now also walks pnpm''s virtual store (node_modules/.pnpm/<pkg>@ver/\n  node_modules/<pkg> — where TRANSITIVE deps actually live) and the bun install cache\n  (.bun/install/cache), deduped by canonical path. Same precise ENTRYPOINT-analyzer pass,\n  which is FP-safe (the residual analyzer FPs were non-entrypoint generated parser files).\n- New scan_build_output pass over .output/.next/dist/build, using a new STRICT\n  CampaignAnalyzer::hidden_payload — the `_$_hex`/MDy DECODER only (a base64-impossible\n  identifier). NOT the version-tag marker (legit UMD libs assign `global.X = require`, e.g.\n  chai — a real FP found and dropped), NOT padding/entropy (prettier''s generated Flow parser\n  FP''d via a padding run). Verified 0 hits across the 832-file legit-bundle corpus.\n\nTests: hidden_payload decoder-only + FP guards; build-output detected; legit build output\nsilent; transitive pnpm dep detected. Re-scan of 3 real projects (full pnpm store + build\noutput) = 0 findings. Full workspace green, clippy clean.","tree":{"sha":"797964e0036ff0f7c89ca3d23e22f2e0563836e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/797964e0036ff0f7c89ca3d23e22f2e0563836e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/a69e61690234f8daf7dd2da9f44da5df35771d56","verification":{"payload":"tree 797964e0036ff0f7c89ca3d23e22f2e0563836e5\nparent d2a40fa14dbaab31a819f3a1bf6e4ec096a1503f\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784640774 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784640774 +0300\n\nfeat(core): scan the hiding spots — pnpm .pnpm store, bun cache, build output (FP-clean)\n\nCloses the \"malware hides in cache/build dirs\" gap the FP hunt raised — WITHOUT the\nstructural-FP flood that made those dirs excluded in the first place (a probe showed\n452/832 legit bundles trip the capability gate).\n\n- scan_node_modules now also walks pnpm''s virtual store (node_modules/.pnpm/<pkg>@ver/\n  node_modules/<pkg> — where TRANSITIVE deps actually live) and the bun install cache\n  (.bun/install/cache), deduped by canonical path. Same precise ENTRYPOINT-analyzer pass,\n  which is FP-safe (the residual analyzer FPs were non-entrypoint generated parser files).\n- New scan_build_output pass over .output/.next/dist/build, using a new STRICT\n  CampaignAnalyzer::hidden_payload — the `_$_hex`/MDy DECODER only (a base64-impossible\n  identifier). NOT the version-tag marker (legit UMD libs assign `global.X = require`, e.g.\n  chai — a real FP found and dropped), NOT padding/entropy (prettier''s generated Flow parser\n  FP''d via a padding run). Verified 0 hits across the 832-file legit-bundle corpus.\n\nTests: hidden_payload decoder-only + FP guards; build-output detected; legit build output\nsilent; transitive pnpm dep detected. Re-scan of 3 real projects (full pnpm store + build\noutput) = 0 findings. Full workspace green, clippy clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal91BhsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPviMQD/Sa/DCmzM6Q0jyQ9P61L5\nAAHE4WUtKMLytET6bTlPtq0A/iVvEbCq2Q5Tc4Lk6rRq6s/b44gEhUhJ3RPz4a4B\nZIwJ\n=1e31\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T13:54:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fati