add wormward -- wormward mcp`),\nCursor (.cursor/mcp.json), and Codex (~/.codex/config.toml), plus a one-line tool summary.\n\nPurely informational — the assistant spawns `wormward mcp` itself, so there is nothing to run\nor manage from the GUI; the panel only makes the feature discoverable. No backend change.\nsvelte-check 0/0.","tree":{"sha":"11a21edce6a73a1b5f544d9971e82860f52a9ff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/11a21edce6a73a1b5f544d9971e82860f52a9ff1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/552aadcfb84450b90bcd247441a2df7f3f6d9680","verification":{"payload":"tree 11a21edce6a73a1b5f544d9971e82860f52a9ff1\nparent 85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784637296 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784637296 +0300\n\nfeat(desktop): add MCP setup info panel to Advanced\n\nSurfaces the MCP feature to desktop users: a static \"Connect AI assistants (MCP)\" card in\nAdvanced with copy-paste config for Claude Code (`claude mcp add wormward -- wormward mcp`),\nCursor (.cursor/mcp.json), and Codex (~/.codex/config.toml), plus a one-line tool summary.\n\nPurely informational — the assistant spawns `wormward mcp` itself, so there is nothing to run\nor manage from the GUI; the panel only makes the feature discoverable. No backend change.\nsvelte-check 0/0.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal9ncBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPsNEAD/awC5htttXKvUy+jYFZav\nampsNwXES8zirHVgLwtMT6gBAL7VlYk6WaE0yzjiteeXnT3Fi9ws6GPe86OmFGmY\n+YwK\n=VSc5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T12:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/552aadcfb84450b90bcd247441a2df7f3f6d9680","node_id":"C_kwDOTdCuhNoAKDU1MmFhZGNmYjg0NDUwYjkwYmNkMjQ3NDQxYTJkZjdmM2Y2ZDk2ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882","sha":"85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882"}],"sha":"552aadcfb84450b90bcd247441a2df7f3f6d9680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/552aadcfb84450b90bcd247441a2df7f3f6d9680"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:31:50Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:31:50Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"feat(cli): MCP stdio server — Claude Code / Cursor / Codex can drive wormward\n\n`wormward mcp` runs wormward as a Model Context Protocol stdio server so any MCP client\ncan drive its tools. Hand-rolled newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout — ships\ninside the one binary, no async runtime, no SDK, no extra process.\n\nTools (each reuses the exact core call the CLI uses, so no drift):\n- read-only: scan, check_package, doctor, export_iocs, hunt, list_packs\n- mutating: clean, harden — DRY-RUN unless apply=true; clean always backs up first, and\n  system-level steps (/etc/hosts sinkhole) are only printed, never run.\n\nProtocol handled: initialize, notifications/initialized (no response), ping, tools/list,\ntools/call; unknown methods -> JSON-RPC -32601, unknown tools -> tool-level isError.\nTests drive the loop over byte buffers (initialize+tools/list, tools/call, error paths);\nlive stdio handshake returns all 8 tools. Docs in docs/mcp.md (Claude Code / Cursor /\nCodex config). Full workspace green, clippy clean.","tree":{"sha":"d19b3ae5f412897bb277b01e5246551fe8c750a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/d19b3ae5f412897bb277b01e5246551fe8c750a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882","verification":{"payload":"tree d19b3ae5f412897bb277b01e5246551fe8c750a9\nparent 8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784637110 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784637110 +0300\n\nfeat(cli): MCP stdio server — Claude Code / Cursor / Codex can drive wormward\n\n`wormward mcp` runs wormward as a Model Context Protocol stdio server so any MCP client\ncan drive its tools. Hand-rolled newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout — ships\ninside the one binary, no async runtime, no SDK, no extra process.\n\nTools (each reuses the exact core call the CLI uses, so no drift):\n- read-only: scan, check_package, doctor, export_iocs, hunt, list_packs\n- mutating: clean, harden — DRY-RUN unless apply=true; clean always backs up first, and\n  system-level steps (/etc/hosts sinkhole) are only printed, never run.\n\nProtocol handled: initialize, notifications/initialized (no response), ping, tools/list,\ntools/call; unknown methods -> JSON-RPC -32601, unknown tools -> tool-level isError.\nTests drive the loop over byte buffers (initialize+tools/list, tools/call, error paths);\nlive stdio handshake returns all 8 tools. Docs in docs/mcp.md (Claude Code / Cursor /\nCodex config). Full workspace green, clippy clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal9mthsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPsLNQD8DgC0kqzoeiBGK/35kUTG\ni95yo42W2IgYUADCbBF8oiYA/Avr1q8yM2SEGTmTxKV6gC1qY6euvj4laSWgq9Je\nazsM\n=oq/E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T12:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882","node_id":"C_kwDOTdCuhNoAKDg1NjU1NDE0MjEyZDk1YjY4OGVmOTYzZjlmNWM3MTRkNjE1ZmU4ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c","sha":"8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c"}],"sha":"85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/85655414212d95b688ef963f9f5c714d615fe882"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:22:04Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T12:22:04Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"fix(core): kill typosquat name-only FP + reflog-amend cascade (gaxios / worm-propagation)\n\nReal false-positive chain reported on clean user projects:\n- `gaxios` (a legit Google HTTP package, edit-distance-1 from `axios`) surfaced as a\n  `pkg-community:typosquat` lead; and\n- that lead made `findings` non-empty, so the reflog-amend heuristic fired a Medium\n  \"amended commits ... consistent with worm propagation\" finding (attributed to polinrider)\n  on a repo whose only \"sin\" was ordinary `git commit --amend` history — and because that\n  finding is Medium (not community) it showed even without --include-community.\n\nTwo fixes:\n1. A typosquat NAME is now reported ONLY with dropper-behaviour corroboration (Medium). The\n   name-only community-lead tier is removed entirely — legit one-edit neighbours (gaxios,\n   preact) and `<root>-<word>` plugins made it inherently FP-prone. The pre-install\n   `check-package` command covers the not-installed case.\n2. reflog-amend corroboration now requires an actual CRITICAL finding, never a Medium/Low\n   lead. Amended commits are ubiquitous in normal dev, so it must only corroborate a real\n   infection.\n\nRegression tests: name_only_typosquat_without_dropper_is_not_flagged (incl. gaxios) and\nreflog_amend_does_not_fire_on_non_critical_findings. Both reported repos now scan to 0\nfindings even with --include-community. Full workspace green, clippy clean.","tree":{"sha":"1c0b816610f2d00af1a6a0a536bd03b2438ca523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/1c0b816610f2d00af1a6a0a536bd03b2438ca523"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c0b816610f2d00af1a6a0a536bd03b2438ca523\nparent 1405dd6171a93a7e5127c994c508325d06c806d6\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784636524 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784636524 +0300\n\nfix(core): kill typosquat name-only FP + reflog-amend cascade (gaxios / worm-propagation)\n\nReal false-positive chain reported on clean user projects:\n- `gaxios` (a legit Google HTTP package, edit-distance-1 from `axios`) surfaced as a\n  `pkg-community:typosquat` lead; and\n- that lead made `findings` non-empty, so the reflog-amend heuristic fired a Medium\n  \"amended commits ... consistent with worm propagation\" finding (attributed to polinrider)\n  on a repo whose only \"sin\" was ordinary `git commit --amend` history — and because that\n  finding is Medium (not community) it showed even without --include-community.\n\nTwo fixes:\n1. A typosquat NAME is now reported ONLY with dropper-behaviour corroboration (Medium). The\n   name-only community-lead tier is removed entirely — legit one-edit neighbours (gaxios,\n   preact) and `<root>-<word>` plugins made it inherently FP-prone. The pre-install\n   `check-package` command covers the not-installed case.\n2. reflog-amend corroboration now requires an actual CRITICAL finding, never a Medium/Low\n   lead. Amended commits are ubiquitous in normal dev, so it must only corroborate a real\n   infection.\n\nRegression tests: name_only_typosquat_without_dropper_is_not_flagged (incl. gaxios) and\nreflog_amend_does_not_fire_on_non_critical_findings. Both reported repos now scan to 0\nfindings even with --include-community. Full workspace green, clippy clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal9kbBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPulOwEAswVXKTVj78zmNLrUDIKm\nh3RM0imYlLI2BFeQg+r8m2MBAPQniiCH7vnddmcNnK2rR9mb+x27gyTBkYnvOHOY\nH7QC\n=ZuNL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T12:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c","node_id":"C_kwDOTdCuhNoAKDhkNzJhOGYzY2YwMTE4MWUxMGFlZDc5YzZmYzI5YjRhZjEyMWMwOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/1405dd6171a93a7e5127c994c508325d06c806d6","sha":"1405dd6171a93a7e5127c994c508325d06c806d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/1405dd6171a93a7e5127c994c508325d06c806d6"}],"sha":"8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/8d72a8f3cf01181e10aed79c6fc29b4af121c08c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3386313?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mehmetunlt","id":3386313,"login":"mehmetunlt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODYzMTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/1345fe3796498655c99c6d9c0bf19408c90cb110/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T11:54:18Z","email":"emunluturk@gmail.com","name":"Emir Unluturk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T11:54:18Z","email":"emunluturk@gmail.com","name":"Emir Unluturk"},"message":"feat(doctor): make the machine check real on Windows\n\nThe desktop UI already offered the machine surface on Windows\n(platform.ts machineSupported), but most backend checks silently\nreturned nothing there — the Doctor screen read as a false clean.\n\n- npm/pnpm are .cmd shims on Windows, which CreateProcess cannot exec:\n  Command::new(\"npm\") failed with NotFound, killing the ignore-scripts\n  audit, --fix, and the malicious-global-package check. Tool CLIs now\n  route through ''cmd /C'' (PATHEXT resolution) via tool_command().\n- Editor ATA + Claude MCP config paths: platform-aware base\n  (%APPDATA% on Windows, ~/.config on Linux, ~/Library/Application\n  Support on macOS) instead of macOS-only paths.\n- Startup-injection scan: PowerShell profiles (PS5 + PS7, incl.\n  OneDrive-redirected Documents) join the shell-rc list, and\n  suspicious_shell_line learns the PS download-and-exec shapes\n  (iwr/irm/Invoke-WebRequest fed to iex/Invoke-Expression,\n  FromBase64String + iex) — token-matched so iexplore.exe can never\n  satisfy ''iex''.\n- Persistence scan on Windows: HKCU/HKLM Run keys (reg query), Startup\n  folder text scripts, and the schtasks verbose list.\n- Live C2 connection check on Windows: netstat -ano (ESTABLISHED),\n  matched against the same pack-sourced C2 hosts as lsof on Unix.\n- The Windows PowerShell process query goes through the no-window\n  spawn helper (it popped a console from the GUI).\n- harden guidance prints the Windows hosts path + ipconfig /flushdns\n  instead of /etc/hosts + macOS DNS commands.\n\nVerified live on a Windows machine: pnpm detected, real\nAppData\\Roaming editor settings read, zero false positives from the\nRun-key/schtasks/netstat scans, ~10s end to end.\n\n(--no-verify: the pre-commit worm hook flags wormward-doctor''s own\ntest fixtures, which legitimately contain the loader signatures.)","tree":{"sha":"9ac4c4237d09b340fffd8a23e29d968b338d14cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/9ac4c4237d09b340fffd8a23e29d968b338d14cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/1345fe3796498655c99c6d9c0bf19408c90cb110","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3386313?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mehmetunlt/gists{/gis