epo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/cafa2109308e8c3d022affa4738f83d0878a7b0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T08:22:13Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T08:22:13Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"docs(readme): record PolinRider GitHub corpus (762 infected) for detection development\n\nAn IOC-seeded, rate-limit-paced, clone-free GitHub sweep. Documents the corpus that\ndrove the version-independence + repo-wide structural hardening: methodology, stats\n(762 confirmed infected; 643 by scan, 121 dropper-only), the observed version-tag\nfamilies (5-3-* is a minority; 8-*/9-*/10-* dominate), and the ~14% non-config-source\nfinding. Full victim list in a collapsed block; framed as a detection-development\nrecord, not a shame list (most are victims of a malicious npm dependency).","tree":{"sha":"385aac10b49dff1b0d9c5af2f4614b7e15f78ddc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/385aac10b49dff1b0d9c5af2f4614b7e15f78ddc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/cafa2109308e8c3d022affa4738f83d0878a7b0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 385aac10b49dff1b0d9c5af2f4614b7e15f78ddc\nparent c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784622133 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784622133 +0300\n\ndocs(readme): record PolinRider GitHub corpus (762 infected) for detection development\n\nAn IOC-seeded, rate-limit-paced, clone-free GitHub sweep. Documents the corpus that\ndrove the version-independence + repo-wide structural hardening: methodology, stats\n(762 confirmed infected; 643 by scan, 121 dropper-only), the observed version-tag\nfamilies (5-3-* is a minority; 8-*/9-*/10-* dominate), and the ~14% non-config-source\nfinding. Full victim list in a collapsed block; framed as a detection-development\nrecord, not a shame list (most are victims of a malicious npm dependency).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal8sNRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPsA5wEAlJ2j/CeAE14xAhbfafjx\n9CH6heGTgChMR8DZWaNMV6sA+gP/OqvGI9VAkd8L/QQaNXOOJYssCvXOknH6Guiz\nKc0A\n=vC5/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T08:23:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/cafa2109308e8c3d022affa4738f83d0878a7b0c","node_id":"C_kwDOTdCuhNoAKGNhZmEyMTA5MzA4ZThjM2QwMjJhZmZhNDczOGY4M2QwODc4YTdiMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9","sha":"c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9"}],"sha":"cafa2109308e8c3d022affa4738f83d0878a7b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/cafa2109308e8c3d022affa4738f83d0878a7b0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T08:20:41Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T08:20:41Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"feat(core): repo-wide structural injection scan — catch payloads in non-config source\n\nA GitHub IOC-seeded sweep (762 confirmed-infected repos) showed ~14% carried the\npayload only in arbitrary executable source — server.js, routes/*.js, Gruntfile.js,\n.prettierrc.mjs, controllers, entry points — never a recognized config. The\nsurface/target passes only read known configs + entry files, so these were missed.\n\nAdd scan_injection_structure: a repo-wide pass over every non-excluded, non-binary\ncode file that fires on capability::injected_payload (a >=200-space padding-run line\nor a _$_hex decoder identifier). Both tells are FP-safe by construction — minified/\ngenerated/vendored output is excluded and has no whitespace runs, and _$_[0-9a-f]{4,}\ncannot occur in base64. Findings are attributed to polinrider as Analyzer, remediable\nvia the existing structural strip, and deduped against surface findings.\n\nCorpus impact: wormward-detected repos 573 -> 643 (rest are dropper-only, caught by\nthe temp_auto_push.bat artifact). Only residual source miss is a payload inside a\nvendor/ dir (intentionally excluded as third-party code).\n\nThe sweep also confirmed the campaign rotates version tags heavily (5-3-* is a\nminority; 8-*/9-*/10-* dominate), vindicating structure-over-constant detection.\n\nTDD: detection on non-config source, minified/build-output FP-safety, surface dedup,\nand a full detect->clean->rescan e2e. Full workspace green; core+packs clippy clean.","tree":{"sha":"4a88f086da7aed10c2331f30165e6f0fe7cd698d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/4a88f086da7aed10c2331f30165e6f0fe7cd698d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a88f086da7aed10c2331f30165e6f0fe7cd698d\nparent 280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784622041 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784622041 +0300\n\nfeat(core): repo-wide structural injection scan — catch payloads in non-config source\n\nA GitHub IOC-seeded sweep (762 confirmed-infected repos) showed ~14% carried the\npayload only in arbitrary executable source — server.js, routes/*.js, Gruntfile.js,\n.prettierrc.mjs, controllers, entry points — never a recognized config. The\nsurface/target passes only read known configs + entry files, so these were missed.\n\nAdd scan_injection_structure: a repo-wide pass over every non-excluded, non-binary\ncode file that fires on capability::injected_payload (a >=200-space padding-run line\nor a _$_hex decoder identifier). Both tells are FP-safe by construction — minified/\ngenerated/vendored output is excluded and has no whitespace runs, and _$_[0-9a-f]{4,}\ncannot occur in base64. Findings are attributed to polinrider as Analyzer, remediable\nvia the existing structural strip, and deduped against surface findings.\n\nCorpus impact: wormward-detected repos 573 -> 643 (rest are dropper-only, caught by\nthe temp_auto_push.bat artifact). Only residual source miss is a payload inside a\nvendor/ dir (intentionally excluded as third-party code).\n\nThe sweep also confirmed the campaign rotates version tags heavily (5-3-* is a\nminority; 8-*/9-*/10-* dominate), vindicating structure-over-constant detection.\n\nTDD: detection on non-config source, minified/build-output FP-safety, surface dedup,\nand a full detect->clean->rescan e2e. Full workspace green; core+packs clippy clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal8r2RsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPv6aAEAtH4Xffkc+m05jTwUVoka\nCc++J1IHgRAJkYAowmzZ1DAA/3upxM5rmoV2JdVrMUlrA6X1E0WqONQO6JW0xI14\nx0gO\n=pqzR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T08:23:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9","node_id":"C_kwDOTdCuhNoAKGM4ZmQ4NmY5ZTQ0ZDQ4YjI2ZGFkNTNkYjNmMjBmMDVhZTBhZDliZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commit/280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c","sha":"280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c"}],"sha":"c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/c8fd86f9e44d48b26dad53db3f20f05ae0ad9be9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/commits/280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T07:27:43Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T07:27:43Z","email":"0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com","name":"0fatihyildiz"},"message":"feat(core): version-independent structural detection — catch mutated PolinRider waves\n\nA new wave rotated its per-version constants (5-3-235→5-3-168, _$_8e2c→_$_3317,\nseed 3899501→3657078) and re-infected repos were reported CLEAN. Root cause was\ntwo enumerated allowlists at the FILE-selection layer — the pack''s target_files\nand classify()''s config-stem list — that both missed the family''s newly-targeted\nfiles (metro.config.js, app.config.ts, seed.ts, migrate.ts). The capability gate\nalso required a plaintext behavioral capability, which a padded blob conceals.\n\nDetect by STRUCTURE, not per-version constants:\n- capability.rs: padding_injection detector (\\S…[ \\t]{200,}…\\S line) as a\n  self-evident worm tell — fires even when behavior is concealed in the blob.\n  FP-safe by construction (minifiers strip whitespace; lockfiles are short lines;\n  base64/WASM has no run-then-code). Shared with the analyzer via one predicate.\n- surface.rs: any *.config.{js,cjs,mjs,ts} is a ConfigFile surface (+ seed/migrate\n  scripts); a clean config of any name still never fires (gate needs a prior/tell).\n  Exclude *.map, *-index.json, public/assets/, Capacitor native mirrors.\n- pack.yaml: *.config.* glob targets replace the per-name allowlist.\n- analyzer.rs: structural padding confirm path (survives decoder/marker rotation);\n  JS-code-token veto and base64/WASM FP guards kept.\n- remediate.rs: remove the createRequire shim only if no genuine require( remains\n  (keep legit ESM interop); strip stays structural (≥200-space run cut).\n\nPer-version literals remain only as attribution, never sole detection.\n\nAcceptance: 5-3-168/_$_3317 and a hypothetical 5-3-999-zz payload are DETECTED and\nCLEANED across the expanded file set and non-default branch tips (--deep); minified\nbundles, yarn.lock, public/assets copies, and @rive-app WASM .mjs are NOT. Full\nworkspace green; core+packs clippy clean.","tree":{"sha":"1a65bb2842fdab4cd8bb949d1535e21cb00cbdc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/trees/1a65bb2842fdab4cd8bb949d1535e21cb00cbdc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0fatihyildiz/wormward/git/commits/280da0aeee04c4a47cee1f0a8f0a49b198faa43c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a65bb2842fdab4cd8bb949d1535e21cb00cbdc8\nparent ac374b838496c7022f0bbd903272f82689423e9b\nauthor 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784618863 +0300\ncommitter 0fatihyildiz <0m.fatih.yildiz@gmail.com> 1784618863 +0300\n\nfeat(core): version-independent structural detection — catch mutated PolinRider waves\n\nA new wave rotated its per-version constants (5-3-235→5-3-168, _$_8e2c→_$_3317,\nseed 3899501→3657078) and re-infected repos were reported CLEAN. Root cause was\ntwo enumerated allowlists at the FILE-selection layer — the pack''s target_files\nand classify()''s config-stem list — that both missed the family''s newly-targeted\nfiles (metro.config.js, app.config.ts, seed.ts, migrate.ts). The capability gate\nalso required a plaintext behavioral capability, which a padded blob conceals.\n\nDetect by STRUCTURE, not per-version constants:\n- capability.rs: padding_injection detector (\\S…[ \\t]{200,}…\\S line) as a\n  self-evident worm tell — fires even when behavior is concealed in the blob.\n  FP-safe by construction (minifiers strip whitespace; lockfiles are short lines;\n  base64/WASM has no run-then-code). Shared with the analyzer via one predicate.\n- surface.rs: any *.config.{js,cjs,mjs,ts} is a ConfigFile surface (+ seed/migrate\n  scripts); a clean config of any name still never fires (gate needs a prior/tell).\n  Exclude *.map, *-index.json, public/assets/, Capacitor native mirrors.\n- pack.yaml: *.config.* glob targets replace the per-name allowlist.\n- analyzer.rs: structural padding confirm path (survives decoder/marker rotation);\n  JS-code-token veto and base64/WASM FP guards kept.\n- remediate.rs: remove the createRequire shim only if no genuine require( remains\n  (keep legit ESM interop); strip stays structural (≥200-space run cut).\n\nPer-version literals remain only as attribution, never sole detection.\n\nAcceptance: 5-3-168/_$_3317 and a hypothetical 5-3-999-zz payload are DETECTED and\nCLEANED across the expanded file set and non-default branch tips (--deep); minified\nbundles, yarn.lock, public/assets copies, and @rive-app WASM .mjs are NOT. Full\nworkspace green; core+packs clippy clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRAwsmkzWs0rQrK0p5Suva06+IE+wUCal8fbxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQUrr2tOviBPtCCQD/aB92ILOdEEZyKdzt7/cG\nEQKsin1EwwpgN64rxVbyG0ABAIzemqTjUJnq27uw0/J6xx21cfUb4axc+8phYqZc\nWFoA\n=uD/S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T07:55:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47571500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0fatihyildiz","id":47571500,"login":"0fatihyildiz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTcxNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0fatihyildiz/starred{/o